  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Correctness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The agent fixed both aborts: the diff capture now treats exit 1 as 'differs' and still aborts on exit 2 or higher, and the owner pipeline gets a scoped `|| true` so an unowned template shows as unassigned; a small gap is that `|| true` on the whole pipeline would also hide a real grep error (exit 2), but this does not trip either cap condition."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "The diff touches only those two lines in scripts/check-drift.sh; the data, workflow and MISSING handling are untouched, drift still fails the job, and the agent noted the deploy-only-file gap instead of fixing it unasked."
      },
      {
        "name": "Explanation",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The reply names the real failure mode: under set -euo pipefail, diff exits 1 on differing files and grep exits 1 on no match (carried through the pipeline by pipefail), and either one aborts the script. It also says what the user lost (no DRIFT line, no summary, later files never checked) and is honest about what it did and did not test."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 9.2
  },
